tortoise-wow: VMaNGOS Eluna gets the Loot, ItemTemplate and Roll types and the
methods a loot script needs.

New userdata types (new files methods/VMangos/LootMethods.h,
ItemTemplateMethods.h and RollMethods.h, registered in methods/Methods.cpp):

- Loot: GetMoney, SetMoney (zero closes the coin in open loot windows),
  GetUnlootedCount, SetUnlootedCount, GetLootType, Clear, GetItems,
  GetQuestItems (tables { id, index, count, needs_quest, is_looted, is_blocked,
  freeforall, is_underthreshold, roll_winner_guid }) and SetItemLooted. A Loot
  is a member of its Creature and the userdata is call-scoped like every other:
  only valid during the call that pushed it, fetch it again with
  Creature:GetLoot.
- ItemTemplate: this pin registered no type for VMaNGOS, so the global
  GetItemTemplate and Item:GetItemTemplate pushed nil ("missing metatable").
  The type is registered with read-only getters (GetItemId, GetName, GetQuality,
  GetClass, GetSubClass, GetFlags, GetSellPrice, GetBuyPrice, GetBuyCount,
  GetInventoryType, GetItemLevel, GetRequiredLevel, GetBonding, GetMaxStackSize,
  GetDisplayId, GetAllowableClass, GetAllowableRace). Item:GetTemplate is an
  alias of Item:GetItemTemplate.
- Roll plus PLAYER_EVENT_ON_GROUP_ROLL_REWARD_ITEM (56, the id ALE uses),
  called (event, player, item, count, voteType, roll) by the core after a need or
  greed winner got the item. The Roll is deleted right after the hook.

New methods: Creature:GetLoot, Creature:AllLootRemovedFromCorpse,
Player:IsAtGroupRewardDistance, Player:IsAtLootRewardDistance,
Player:IsBot (headless session, or ScriptMgr::IsBotManaged), Unit:GetCritterGUID
(was a METHOD_REG_NONE stub; the mini pet's guid or nil),
Group:GetMembersOnMap (Group:GetMembers is world-only; this one lists the
members in the world and on the calling state's map, so it works in a map
state), and the globals GetStateMapId (-1 in the world state) and
GetStateInstanceId.

Upstreamable to Eluna as VMaNGOS additions, except Player:IsBot (it asks the
core's script manager) and the two call sites in the core's Group.cpp.

Base: ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna 1b06f28ff3a00054d915d824c725fb4283fee74d (branch
cmangos-spell-update), the dep/Eluna pin, with patches 0001-0010 applied. Eluna is
GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna, LICENSE); this change is under
the same licence. Applied by cmake/ElunaSources.cmake to a copy in the build tree.
